    "durationMs": 290680,
    "finalText": "Implementation complete and fully verified. The workspace now contains a FastAPI URL shortener backed by SQLAlchemy/Alembic on PostgreSQL:\n\n**Structure** — `app/` (config reads `DATABASE_URL` via pydantic-settings, models, schemas, routes), `alembic/` (one migration creating the `links` table), `start.sh`, `requirements.txt` (stack pins), `README.md`, `tests/`.\n\n**Verification results:**\n- `sh start.sh` applies migrations then serves in the foreground on `0.0.0.0:8000`\n- All live HTTP checks passed: 201 create with returned URL unchanged (incl. userinfo/port/case), 409 duplicate with `error`, 404s with `error`, 302 redirect with correct `Location` incrementing clicks exactly once, list in ascending creation order with `items`/`total`, and 422 with `error` for malformed JSON, invalid/missing URLs, and invalid codes (body and path, e.g. 3-char or `bad!code`)\n- Persistence confirmed across a genuine server kill/restart — clicks carried over and kept incrementing\n- `pytest tests` — 7 passed; DB truncated afterward so the external suite starts with 0 rows\n\nCodes are 4–20 chars of `[A-Za-z0-9_-]`; generated codes are 8 random chars with uniqueness checks. Nothing was committed to git, as that wasn't requested."
